    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1288">

                <pb facs="1241" n="1075" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg1075"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.115/316</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">El Paso</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-29T15:00:00-07:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 29, 1917, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My June 29, 11 a.m. Letter from Chihuahua dated 27th just received with
                    information that forced loan was intended to raise five hundred thousand pesos,
                    at present rate of exchange over two hundred and fifty thousand dollars, and
                    that ten parties had then been imprisoned for failure to respond; this included
                    some foreigners.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cobb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
